codex
The complete script passed, but the symbolic negative probes exposed an avoidable Haskell backend `DecidePredicateUnknown` bug and generated a diagnostic archive. I’m tightening both probes to concrete counterexamples (`modp(3,5) ≠ 4` and mutated-base `modp(1,5) ≠ 2`), as the validation contract recommends; this gives cleaner, faster, more reproducible expected failures without changing the symbolic target theorem.
apply patch
